    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_58f8e988",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: found_bigfoot_married_her_obama; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts former U.S. President Barack Obama with a somber expression, overlaid with the text 'found bigfoot' and 'married her.' This meme uses a juxtaposition of a serious political figure with absurd, fictional content to create humor. While not explicitly targeting a protected group with hate or abuse, the meme is harmful because it trivializes the office of the presidency and the dignity of the individual by associating him with a mythical creature and implying a bizarre, non-consensual narrative. The intent is satirical or absurdist humor, but the use of a real political leader in such a context can be seen as disrespectful and potentially damaging to public perception of the office, especially if it is used to mock or undermine his credibility. The meme does not contain direct hate or abuse, but its potential to cause harm lies in its disrespectful portrayal of a national leader, which can contribute to a culture of ridicule and disrespect toward public figures.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6920175b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
